    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine how many minutes it will take for the printer to print 200 pages, we first need to find out the printer's rate and then use that rate to calculate the time required. We find the time by dividing the total number of pages by the rate per minute.\n\n### Step-by-step reasoning:\n\n1. The printer's printing speed is 17 pages per minute.\n2. We need to find out how many minutes it takes to print 200 pages.\n   \nTo calculate this, we can use the formula:\n\\[ \\text{Time (in minutes)} = \\frac{\\text{Total page count}} {\\text{Rate}} \\]\n\n### Calculation:\n\n3. Substitute the given values into the formula:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Time (in minutes)} = \\frac{200}\\{17\\}\n   \\]\n   \n4. By dividing 200 by 17, we obtain approximately 11.76 minutes. Since the final time needs to be nearest to whole number:\n   \n5. Round the result to the nearest whole number:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Time (rounded)} = 12 \\text{ minutes}\n   \\]\n\nThus, taking into account all steps in the reasoning process, the answer is: \n\n\\boxed{12}",
